cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Value-Field Theory (VFT)"
message: "If you use this theory or repository, please cite this repository."
authors:
  - family-names: "Nuno"
    given-names: "T."
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
abstract: >
  Value-Field Theory (VFT) is a structural framework for describing how
  actor-relative, multidimensional real resource and capital states K and
  nominal or expectation structures P form a value field whose attraction is
  realized through actors' actions and decisions A. Each actor can access a
  different K and observe or reference a different P. P is treated as a
  history-dependent expectation stock, while E[Delta K] is represented
  separately as an expectation flow for a specified interval rather than as a
  required intermediate variable in action generation. In economic
  projections, interactions among actors' expected Delta K and actions can be
  mapped to existing microeconomic equilibrium processes, while aggregate
  macroeconomic adjustment can be represented as interaction between the
  previous interval's realized Delta K on the real side and current Delta P on
  the nominal or expectation side. Delta P can serve as an intervention path
  across observation scales; at the state level, interest-rate and money-supply
  operations are representative mappings. These equilibrium mechanisms are not
  defined as VFT-specific universal laws. Actions can change both K and P,
  while non-agentic changes to K such as depreciation or natural loss are
  treated only as an exception note. At aggregate scales, Delta P and Delta K
  can serve as principal proxies when full action tracking is too costly.
repository-code: "https://github.com/nuno929/vf-model"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
keywords:
